{# Shared sentence-pattern macros for the Insightful 4.0 pipeline templates.
   Each macro takes a Signal object and emits 1-2 sentences of editorial prose.
   Voice target: "A senior furniture-industry consultant wrote this for a furniture CEO."
   Rules: no invented causation, no metaphors-as-analysis, lead with dollar and name.

   CLIENT-FACING LABEL DICTIONARY (2026-07-13 voice pass) — use these words in
   client HTML; keep internal names only in Jinja comments / code:
     GMV                    → eCat orders (confirmed) / order dollars
     dollar retention / NRR → same dealers spent $X for every $1 last year
     fully churned          → went dark / stopped buying
     contribution proxy     → (omit from hero; say "up/down $X" if needed)
     lifters / decliners    → accounts that grew / accounts that shrank
     capture rate           → (never as a client headline; absolute $ only)
     posture / pipeline     → never in client prose
     feed                   → invoice data / order data (when you must name it)
#}

{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   SENTENCE-PATTERN MACROS — one per SignalKind (13 total)
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}

{# ─── real_decline ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_real_decline(sig, account) -%}
{{ account.bill_to_name or account.bill_to_number or "(unnamed)" }} — ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(account.ltm_rev / 1000) }}K invoiced (LTM) — is down {{ "{:.0f}".format((1 - account.recent_6mo / account.prior_6mo) * 100) if account.prior_6mo > 0 else "materially" }}% over the last six months and {% if account.days_silent > 30 %}has gone {{ account.days_silent }} days silent{% else %}is still ordering{% endif %}. The slope is unambiguous; the cause needs a phone call.
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── cadence_cliff ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_cadence_cliff(sig, account) -%}
{{ account.bill_to_name or account.bill_to_number or "(unnamed)" }} — ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(account.ltm_rev / 1000) }}K invoiced (LTM) — skipped a beat: {{ account.days_silent }} days silent against a {{ "{:.0f}".format(account.mean_order_gap_days) }}-day normal cadence, but the account {% if account.recent_vs_prior_pct is not none and account.recent_vs_prior_pct > 0 %}is up {{ "{:.0f}".format(account.recent_vs_prior_pct) }}% year-over-year{% else %}is not declining{% endif %}. Confirm the next order is still coming; do not open a decline conversation on a growing book.
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── growth_pocket ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_growth_pocket(sig, family) -%}
The {{ family.family_label }} family is up {{ "{:+.0f}".format(family.yoy_pct) }}% YoY — ${{ "{:,.2f}".format(family.ltm_revenue / 1_000_000) }}M invoiced (LTM) across {{ family.dealer_count }} dealers on {{ family.sku_count }} SKUs. That distribution is product depth, not product luck — broad enough to survive a single soft market.
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── new_line_takeoff ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_new_line_takeoff(sig, family) -%}
{{ family.family_label }} cleared ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(family.ltm_revenue / 1000) }}K across {{ family.dealer_count }} dealers in its first full year. A new line that clears six figures across that many dealers in year one is earning its floor space on merit, not on introductory pricing.
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── lift_concentration ──────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_lift_concentration(sig, probe) -%}
Your top customer holds {{ "{:.0f}".format(probe.top1_share) }}% of LTM invoiced revenue (HHI {{ "{:.0f}".format(probe.hhi) }}). {% if probe.top1_share >= 25 %}That is structural concentration — a single account decision moves the topline.{% else %}Worth watching — not crisis-level, but a single account's buying cadence will show up in your quarterly results.{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── rep_overperform ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_rep_overperform(sig, rep) -%}
{{ rep.display_label or rep.rep_label or ("rep " ~ rep.rep_number) }} grew {{ "{:+.0f}".format(rep.yoy_pct) }}% year-over-year — ${{ "{:,.2f}".format(rep.ltm_invoiced / 1_000_000) }}M invoiced (LTM) across {{ rep.customer_count }} accounts. That is a field build, not a one-account windfall.
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── rep_underperform ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_rep_underperform(sig, rep) -%}
{{ rep.display_label or rep.rep_label or ("rep " ~ rep.rep_number) }} is down {{ "{:.0f}".format(rep.yoy_pct | abs) }}% year-over-year on a ${{ "{:,.2f}".format(rep.ltm_invoiced / 1_000_000) }}M book ({{ rep.customer_count }} accounts). The territory needs a coverage review — a book-wide decline across that many accounts is structural, not one bad break.
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── rep_atrisk_book ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_rep_atrisk_book(sig, risk) -%}
{% if risk.accounts_at_risk and risk.accounts_at_risk > 0 -%}
{{ risk.display_label or risk.rep_name_tier2 or ("rep " ~ risk.rep_number) }} carries ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(risk.dollars_at_risk / 1000) }}K flagged across {{ risk.accounts_at_risk }} account{{ "s" if risk.accounts_at_risk != 1 else "" }}{% if risk.leak_pct is not none %} ({{ "{:.1f}".format(risk.leak_pct) }}% leak rate on the book){% endif %}. Read the slope on the flagged account before choosing the call shape.
{%- else -%}
{{ risk.display_label or risk.rep_name_tier2 or ("rep " ~ risk.rep_number) }} shows ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(risk.dollars_at_risk / 1000) }}K of exposure{% if risk.leak_pct is not none %} at a {{ "{:.1f}".format(risk.leak_pct) }}% leak rate{% endif %} — discount-discipline bleed, not account decay (no single account crossed the at-risk threshold). Review discount authority on this book rather than one account.
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── cross_sell_pocket ────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_cross_sell_pocket(sig) -%}
Dealers buying {{ sig.context.anchor }} have never ordered from the {{ sig.context.target }} family — same buyer profile, same floor, already pre-qualified by their own buying history. Push the list to the field this week and ask for a quote inside 30 days.
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── second_year_gap ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_second_year_gap(sig, dealers) -%}
Only {{ "{:.0f}".format(dealers.second_year_return_rate * 100) }}% of first-time buyers came back for a second year. You are winning new accounts at the front door and losing them at the back. Every 5-point move on that return rate is meaningful dollars on the full new-dealer base.
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── channel_concentration ────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_channel_concentration(sig, channel) -%}
{{ channel.label }} accounts for {{ "{:.0f}".format(channel.share_pct) }}% of booked revenue (${{ "{:,.2f}".format(channel.booked_dollars / 1_000_000) }}M LTM). A single channel decision — a fee change, an algorithm shift, a buyer rotation — moves the topline at that concentration level.
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── ecat_minority ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{# ─── single_door_project (P0-7) ───────────────────────────────────────────
   A custom project is not catalog volume. Left unnamed it does two things at
   once: it crowds the real catalog story out of the top-12 table, and it hides
   the more interesting fact — that one door and one project carried a material
   slice of the year. Say it first, then read the catalog without it. #}
{% macro signal_single_door_project(sig) -%}
{%- set c = sig.context -%}
{# Two paragraphs on purpose: the renderer lifts the FIRST paragraph of a
   section into its summary card, and a single long one truncates mid-clause. #}
**{{ c.sku_count }} of the items below share the {{ c.prefix }} prefix and went to a single dealer — ${{ "{:,.2f}".format(c.dollars / 1_000_000) }}M invoiced (LTM), {{ "{:.1f}".format(c.share_pct) }}% of the year, on {{ c.units }} units.**

At ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(c.unit_price) }} a unit — {{ "{:.0f}".format(c.unit_price_ratio) }}× the median item on this list — that is one project, not a line the field can reorder. The catalog reads differently once you set it aside: everything below it is the repeatable business.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro signal_ecat_minority(sig) -%}
eCat is {{ "{:.1f}".format(sig.context.ecat_pct) }}% of invoiced LTM — a minority of the book for a business that still runs primarily through dealers, trade, and direct. Shown as absolute order dollars, not as a share of "total business" — that claim needs a second independent feed.
{%- endmacro %}

{# ─── leakage_discipline ──────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% macro signal_leakage_discipline(sig) -%}
Org-wide leakage is {{ "{:.1f}".format(sig.context.leak_pct) }}% — well below the 3% industry-normal threshold. Pricing discipline is not the problem here; the dollars at risk are in volume retention, not discount bleed.
{%- endmacro %}


{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   CONFIDENCE HEADERS — deterministic per posture.commerce_confidence
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}

{% macro confidence_header(posture) -%}
{% if posture.commerce_confidence == "STRONG" -%}
Every dollar in this report is a direct result from your invoice data — same method, same window, reproduces exactly. Where a figure is directional (estimated upside, addressable subset), it is flagged inline.
{%- elif posture.commerce_confidence == "PARTIAL" -%}
This report draws from a single invoice source that has not been cross-verified against a second independent view. Dollar figures are real results on real invoices — but "your invoiced business" is the honest framing, not "your total business." Directional figures are flagged where they appear.
{%- elif posture.commerce_confidence == "LIMITED" -%}
Limited commerce signal: invoice data is present but thin (fewer than 1,000 invoices or under $1M LTM). Patterns are real but dollar-impact estimates carry wider margins. Treat specific-account findings as directional leads, not confirmed reads.
{%- elif posture.commerce_confidence == "NONE" -%}
No invoiced dollars available on this window. Findings here are drawn from eCat activity and order-level signals only; no rep-to-revenue claims are made.
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}


{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   §Q SENSITIVITY HEDGE — the deterministic path's half of the gate
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

   §Q requires every Tier-A/S dollar claim to carry an adjacent "what would
   change this read" sentence. On the prose path that sentence is authored
   inside the slot. With no API key and no prose file every slot is skipped,
   the deterministic templates still emit Tier-A dollars, and nothing hedges
   them — which is why bmc (PARTIAL) could not ship at all.

   §Q.3 says the hedge "must be authored, not templated." That holds for the
   prose path, where there is an author. The deterministic fallback has none,
   so its choice is a templated hedge or no hedge, and no hedge means no
   report. The macro therefore does the work §Q.4(a) asks of a collective
   hedge: it NAMES THE UNCERTAINTY CLASS (one un-cross-verified invoice
   source, or a frozen one) instead of stamping a bracket, and it carries the
   §Q.2 marker phrasing verbatim.

   Marker tokens for pipeline.smoke_check._HEDGE_MARKERS: "directional",
   "floor". §Q.2 phrasings: "What would change this read", "pressure-test".
   Do not reword either without re-reading §Q.2 — both gates read this text.
#}

{% macro sensitivity_hedge(posture, subject="The dollars above", singular=false) -%}
What would change this read: {{ subject }} {{ "is" if singular else "are" }} directional — a floor drawn from {% if posture.is_stale %}an invoice feed that stopped updating {{ posture.stale_age_phrase }} ago{% else %}one invoice source that has not been cross-verified against a second independent view{% endif %}. {% if posture.is_stale %}A refreshed feed{% else %}A second source{% endif %} moves the size of these numbers, not their direction; pressure-test the size before you plan against it.
{%- endmacro %}


{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   "WHAT THIS MEANS" / ACTION BLOCKS — per signal type, max 3 sentences
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}

{% macro action_real_decline(account) -%}
**Action:** Investigative call this week — walk the candidate explanations (competitive vendor, buyer change, channel shift, project completion) and bring back a read. The slope is clear; the cause is not.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_cadence_cliff(account) -%}
**Action:** Quick confirm call — not a decline conversation. Verify the next order is still coming; do not flag concern on a growing book.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_growth_pocket(family) -%}
**Action:** Protect the distribution. A growth family across {{ family.dealer_count }} dealers is earning its floor space — the risk now is supply-side (lead times, stock-outs) or field-side (reps not leading with it). Confirm both.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_declining_family(family) -%}
**Action:** Defend the base. {{ family.dealer_count }} dealers on a line down {{ "{:.0f}".format(family.yoy_pct | abs) }}% is still the distribution to protect while the mix resets — the near-term risk is losing floor or shelf space to a competitor during the down cycle. Confirm the line stays merchandised and the field keeps showing it; do not treat the decline as a reason to stop leading with it.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_new_line_takeoff(family) -%}
**Action:** Pour fuel. A new line clearing six figures across {{ family.dealer_count }}+ dealers in year one is the rarest signal in this business — field teams, marketing spend, and production capacity should follow the pull, not wait for it to prove itself again.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_lift_concentration(probe) -%}
**Action:** Map the exposure. Know the top account's contract renewal timeline, buying cadence, and decision-maker stability. Concentration is not a problem to solve — it is a risk to see coming.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_rep_overperform(rep) -%}
**Action:** Protect the territory. A book growing at this rate attracts poaching — internal territory carve-ups, competitive recruitment, or simple burnout. Do not lose this person to neglect.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_rep_underperform(rep) -%}
**Action:** Book a territory review with {{ rep.display_label or rep.rep_label or ("rep " ~ rep.rep_number) }} this week. Look for the cluster pattern — is it one account pulling the average down, or a broad-based fade across the book? Different problems, different fixes.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_rep_atrisk_book(risk, account=none) -%}
{% if account and account.is_real_decline -%}
**Action:** Walk this account this week — the slope is a real decline. One conversation may explain the pattern; if it does not, triage the rest by days-silent and dollar-at-risk.
{%- elif account and (account.is_cadence_cliff or (account.recent_vs_prior_pct is not none and account.recent_vs_prior_pct > 0)) -%}
**Action:** Confirm the next order — keep-pace, not a decline walk. This account is growing; do not open it as an at-risk rescue.
{%- else -%}
**Action:** Light-touch check-in on the flagged account. Do not open a decline conversation unless the slope is a real decline.
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_cross_sell_pocket() -%}
**Action:** Ship the named dealer list to the field this week with a 30-day quote ask. The list is pre-qualified by the dealers' own buying behavior — no cold outreach, no guesswork.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_second_year_gap(dealers) -%}
**Action:** Pick the play — a 60-day reorder check-in, a first-reorder incentive, or a named-rep handoff at day 30 — and run it on the addressable subset. It does not have to be expensive. It has to be deliberate and measured.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_channel_concentration(channel) -%}
**Action:** Map the dependency. Know the top channel's fee structure, algorithm changes, and buyer-rotation cadence. Diversification is the medium-term play; visibility is the immediate one.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_ecat_minority() -%}
**Action:** This is context, not an urgent finding. eCat share is reported for completeness; the business runs through traditional channels and the report's intelligence value is in those channels, not in eCat adoption.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro action_leakage_discipline(has_outlier=false, outlier_rep="", outlier_pct=0) -%}
{% if has_outlier -%}
**Action:** Book a discount-authority review with {{ outlier_rep }} this week. A {{ "{:.0f}".format(outlier_pct) }}% leak rate is wide enough to be a coaching question, not just a policy one. The rest of the rep base is within normal range.
{%- else -%}
**Action:** No pricing-discipline intervention needed. The dollars at risk in this report are volume-side (account decay, cadence gaps) — not discount-side. Focus coaching time accordingly.
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}


{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   T1-1 — HERO FINDING RENDERER
   Renders ONE signal into a "thing you wouldn't have known" line, or nothing
   when the signal has no renderable form for this org.

   Why this exists: the hero used three hardcoded if/elif ladders, each of
   which re-imposed decline-first ordering regardless of what
   signal_summary_set() had arranged. `top_signals` was consulted only as a
   membership test, never as an ordering — so the narrative arc (momentum →
   intelligence → opportunity → risk, >=3 positive, finding #1 positive) could
   not reach the page. The hero now LOOPS this macro over the arc-ordered
   signals and takes the first three that render.

   Every branch states a number and a consequence. No invented causation, no
   meta-commentary about the report's own value.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% macro hero_finding(sig, gather, posture, thresholds) -%}
{%- set c = sig.context -%}
{#- Resolved cross-sell anchor label. Computed HERE, not inside the if-chain: a
    {% set %} between elif branches belongs to the previous branch's body, so the
    name is undefined when that branch did not match. Materialise to lists first —
    under StrictUndefined `| first` on an EMPTY sequence RAISES, and most signal
    kinds carry no `anchor`, so the naive form blew up the whole hero. -#}
{%- set _xs_hits = gather.products | selectattr("item_number", "eq", c.anchor | default("", true)) | map(attribute="display_description") | list -%}
{%- set _xs_all = gather.products | map(attribute="display_description") | list -%}
{%- set _xs_anchor = _xs_hits[0] if _xs_hits else (_xs_all[0] if _xs_all else c.anchor | default("", true)) -%}
{#- ── momentum ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}
{%- if sig.kind == "growth_pocket" and c.family -%}
**The {{ (gather.named_families | selectattr("family_label","eq",c.family) | map(attribute="display_label") | list | first) if (gather.named_families | selectattr("family_label","eq",c.family) | list) else c.family }} family is up {{ "{:.0f}".format(c.yoy) }}% across {{ (gather.named_families | selectattr("family_label","eq",c.family) | map(attribute="dealer_count") | list | first) if (gather.named_families | selectattr("family_label","eq",c.family) | list) else "multiple" }} dealers.** Growth spread that wide is depth in the line, not one dealer loading up.
{%- elif sig.kind == "new_line_takeoff" and c.family -%}
**{{ (gather.named_families | selectattr("family_label","eq",c.family) | map(attribute="display_label") | list | first) if (gather.named_families | selectattr("family_label","eq",c.family) | list) else c.family }} cleared ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(sig.dollar_impact / 1000) }}K in its first year on the invoiced record.** A new line reaching that many floors in year one is a distribution result, not a launch.
{%- elif sig.kind == "rep_overperform" and c.rep -%}
**{{ c.rep }} is up {{ "{:.0f}".format(c.yoy) }}% year over year — ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(sig.dollar_impact / 1000) }}K.** That is field-built growth on a named book; what changed there is worth knowing before anything gets fixed elsewhere.
{#- ── intelligence ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}
{%- elif sig.kind == "single_door_project" and c.sku_count -%}
**{{ c.sku_count }} items sharing the {{ c.prefix }} prefix went to a single dealer — ${{ "{:,.2f}".format(c.dollars / 1_000_000) }}M, {{ "{:.1f}".format(c.share_pct) }}% of the year.** At ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(c.unit_price) }} a unit, {{ "{:.0f}".format(c.unit_price_ratio) }}× the median item, that is one project — not a line the field can reorder.
{%- elif sig.kind == "lift_concentration" and c.top1_pct -%}
**Your top customer holds {{ "{:.0f}".format(c.top1_pct) }}% of LTM revenue.** At that level a single account decision — a buyer rotation, a fee change, a competitor in the door — moves the topline on its own.
{%- elif sig.kind == "leakage_discipline" and c.leak_pct is not none -%}
**Discount leakage runs {{ "{:.1f}".format(c.leak_pct) }}% of invoiced — ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(c.total_leak_dollars / 1000) }}K.** That is disciplined in aggregate; the spread between reps is where the coaching conversation is, not the policy.
{%- elif sig.kind == "channel_concentration" and c.channel and "unmapped" not in (c.channel | lower) and "other" != (c.channel | lower) and "unclassified" not in (c.channel | lower)
      and "unattributed" not in (c.channel | lower) and c.pct < 99.5 -%}
**{{ c.channel }} carries {{ "{:.0f}".format(c.pct) }}% of booked revenue.** One channel decision at that share moves the topline.
{%- elif sig.kind == "ecat_minority" and c.ecat_pct is not none -%}
**Confirmed platform orders are ${{ "{:,.2f}".format(posture.ecat_ltm_confirmed_gmv / 1_000_000) }}M against ${{ "{:,.2f}".format(c.inv_ltm_net / 1_000_000) }}M invoiced.** Both are absolute counts from separate feeds — the point is not the ratio, it is how much is still written where you cannot see the order.
{#- ── opportunity ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}
{#- W3/S1: the stopgap floor of 3 that lived here is GONE. The gate is now
    `thresholds.cross_sell_hero_min_dealers` — max(absolute floor, share of the
    org's own active-dealer base), resolved in signals.py and handed in through
    `availability.thresholds`. A one-door overlap is not "a thing you wouldn't
    have known", and on a 2,422-dealer base neither is a three-door one. -#}
{%- elif sig.kind == "cross_sell_pocket" and c.anchor and c.target and gather.cross_sell_gap and gather.cross_sell_gap.count >= thresholds.cross_sell_hero_min_dealers
      and (c.target | lower) not in (_xs_anchor | lower) -%}
**{{ gather.cross_sell_gap.count }} dealers buy {{ _xs_anchor }} but have never bought from the {{ (gather.named_families | selectattr("family_label","eq",c.target) | map(attribute="display_label") | list | first) if (gather.named_families | selectattr("family_label","eq",c.target) | list) else c.target }} family.** Same buyer, same floor — that is a pre-qualified list, not a catalog theory.
{%- elif sig.kind == "second_year_gap" and gather.dealers and gather.dealers.second_year_return_rate is not none -%}
**{{ "{:,}".format(gather.dealers.new_dealers) }} dealers placed a first-ever order last year. {{ "{:,}".format((gather.dealers.new_dealers * gather.dealers.second_year_return_rate) | int) }} came back.** A {{ "{:.1f}".format(gather.dealers.second_year_return_rate * 100) }}% second-year return rate means you are winning accounts at the front door and losing them at the back.
{#- ── risk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}
{%- elif sig.kind in ("real_decline", "cadence_cliff") and c.account -%}
{%- set acct = gather.decay | selectattr("bill_to_number", "eq", c.account) | first -%}
{%- if acct -%}
{%- if sig.kind == "real_decline" -%}
**{{ acct.bill_to_name or acct.bill_to_number }} — ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(acct.ltm_rev / 1000) }}K LTM — {{ "was" if posture.is_stale else "is" }} down {{ "{:.0f}".format((1 - acct.recent_6mo / acct.prior_6mo) * 100) if acct.prior_6mo > 0 else "materially" }}% in six months{% if acct.days_silent < 14 %} and {{ "was" if posture.is_stale else "is" }} still ordering{% endif %}.** {% if posture.is_stale %}That was the slope as of {{ posture.report_through_date }}; whether it held is exactly what a refreshed feed answers.{% else %}The slope is unambiguous; the cause needs a phone call this week, not a quarter from now.{% endif %}
{%- else -%}
**{{ acct.bill_to_name or acct.bill_to_number }} — ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(acct.ltm_rev / 1000) }}K LTM — skipped a beat: {{ acct.days_silent }} days silent on a {{ "{:.0f}".format(acct.mean_order_gap_days) }}-day cadence, but the account is growing.** Confirm call, not a decline conversation.
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- elif sig.kind == "territory_cluster_decay" and c.rep -%}
**{{ c.accounts }} of the at-risk accounts sit on one book — {{ c.rep }}, ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(c.total_at_risk / 1000) }}K.** A cluster on a single territory is a coverage signal the rep cannot see from the inside; walk the pattern before working the accounts one by one.
{%- elif sig.kind == "rep_atrisk_book" and c.rep -%}
**{{ c.rep }} carries ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(sig.dollar_impact / 1000) }}K at risk on their own book.** That concentration warrants a specific coverage review this week.
{%- elif sig.kind == "rep_underperform" and c.rep -%}
**{{ c.rep }}'s book is down {{ "{:.0f}".format(c.yoy | abs) }}% to ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(sig.dollar_impact / 1000) }}K.** A declining book on a named territory is a coverage conversation before it is a performance one.
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}


{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   TALKING-POINT GENERATOR — for §2 Do-this-week rows
   One-line talking point in conversational form (what the rep says to the
   account on the phone). Voice: direct, named, dollar-grounded.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}

{# talking_point — one line per call row. Varied by signal kind × decline
   magnitude × days-silent bucket so a 7-row list doesn't collapse into the
   same sentence five times (audit_cci §talking-points). Fully deterministic:
   phrasing is driven by the account's own numbers, never randomness, so the
   regression harness stays byte-stable. #}
{% macro talking_point(account, posture) -%}
{%- set d = account.days_silent -%}
{%- set p = account.recent_vs_prior_pct -%}
{%- if account.is_cadence_cliff -%}
{%- if d and d > 60 -%}
"You're up{% if p is not none %} {{ "{:.0f}".format(p) }}%{% endif %} but {{ d }} days past your ~{{ "{:.0f}".format(account.mean_order_gap_days) }}-day reorder rhythm — probably timing. Want to line up the next one?"
{%- else -%}
"Growing account that skipped a beat on a {{ "{:.0f}".format(account.mean_order_gap_days) }}-day cadence. Lead with the reorder, not concern — this one's healthy."
{%- endif -%}
{%- elif account.is_real_decline and p is not none and p <= -45 -%}
{%- if d and d > 90 -%}
"Six months of decline and {{ d }} days dark. Is someone else reworking this account, or did the program change?"
{%- elif d and d > 45 -%}
"Volume has {{ "halved" if p <= -50 else "dropped ~" ~ "{:.0f}".format(p | abs) ~ "%" }} and it's been {{ d }} days. Assortment, price, or a competitor in the door?"
{%- else -%}
"Pace has collapsed {{ "{:.0f}".format(p | abs) }}% in six months. Get ahead of it now, while the relationship is still warm."
{%- endif -%}
{%- elif account.is_real_decline and p is not none and p <= -20 -%}
{%- if d and d > 60 -%}
"Down {{ "{:.0f}".format(p | abs) }}% and quiet {{ d }} days — call before it hardens into a trend. What shifted?"
{%- else -%}
"Ordering is off about {{ "{:.0f}".format(p | abs) }}% over six months. What's changing on your floor?"
{%- endif -%}
{%- elif account.is_real_decline and p is not none -%}
"Running {{ "{:.0f}".format(p | abs) }}% behind last year — early enough to turn around with a check-in. What's the read?"
{%- elif account.is_real_decline -%}
"{{ d }} days since the last order on a formerly steady account. What shifted — timing, or something bigger?"
{%- elif d and d > 60 and (p is none or p <= 5) -%}
"It's been {{ d }} days. What changed — project on hold, or did we lose the slot?"
{%- elif p is not none and p <= -20 -%}
"Ordering is running about {{ "{:.0f}".format(p | abs) }}% behind its recent pace. Worth a direct call — what's shifting?"
{%- elif p is not none and p < -5 -%}
"Pace has eased off {{ "{:.0f}".format(p | abs) }}%. A quick check-in now, before it settles into a trend."
{%- elif p is not none and p > 5 -%}
{%- if d and d <= 7 -%}
"Up {{ "{:+.0f}".format(p) }}% on a ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(account.ltm_rev / 1000) }}K book and ordered {{ d }} day{{ "s" if d != 1 else "" }} ago — keep-pace, not a rescue. What else can we load in?"
{%- elif d and d > 21 -%}
"Still pacing up ({{ "{:+.0f}".format(p) }}%) on ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(account.ltm_rev / 1000) }}K but {{ d }} days quiet. Confirm the next order is on the calendar."
{%- else -%}
"Still pacing up ({{ "{:+.0f}".format(p) }}%) on a ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(account.ltm_rev / 1000) }}K book — reinforce the relationship, not a rescue. What else can we load in?"
{%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
"Ordering pace shifted recently — worth a quick check-in. What's the read on your end?"
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}


