{% macro erp_unlock_block(posture) -%}
## What an invoiced ERP feed would unlock

This brief runs on owned platform data — eCat orders and in-app activity — which is why it leads with rep behavior and digital-channel volume. Connect an invoiced ERP feed and the same engine produces the full CEO intelligence brief:

- **Revenue outcomes by rep and account** — who is growing, who is fading, and the dollars at stake, tied to invoiced net (not booked orders).
- **The at-risk watchlist** — named accounts slowing down, with the dollar at risk and the rep to make the call.
- **Growth families and cross-sell** — which lines are lifting the topline and which dealers are the pre-qualified next buyers.
- **Same-dealer retention and reorder flow** — the reorder engine underneath the headline dealer count.

Until then, the behavior floor above is the honest, live read: real platform activity, no invented revenue.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro stale_ecat_recovery_lead(posture) -%}
**Refresh the feed — then work the live signal.** The invoice feed went quiet **{{ posture.stale_age_phrase }} ago** ({{ posture.erp_asof_stamp }}), so the invoiced numbers in this brief are a snapshot of that frozen window, not a live read. What *is* live: **${{ "{:,.2f}".format(posture.ecat_ltm_confirmed_gmv / 1_000_000) }}M of confirmed eCat order volume — a live floor ({{ posture.ecat_live_stamp }})** — the org is still placing orders through the platform even though the invoice feed stopped. Lead the recovery here:

- **Refresh the invoice feed.** Every historical dollar below re-verifies the moment a current feed lands — that is step one, before any account call.
- **Work the live eCat channel.** ${{ "{:,.2f}".format(posture.ecat_ltm_confirmed_gmv / 1_000_000) }}M is confirmed and current — a live floor on digital activity, and the accounts still ordering there are the recovery base, not the frozen invoice watchlist.
- **Read the decline sections as history.** They describe the business as of {{ posture.report_through_date }}; use them to prioritize *which* relationships to re-confirm once the feed is current.
{%- endmacro %}


